{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in a single deterministic specification with small helper states. The specification is conservative under open-loop motion by forcing obstacle-triggered turn recovery, self-looping non-critical path_clear in commit states, forbidding forward/random motion in obstacle-reached states, and returning quickly to exploration once clear. Coverage is biased by making the initial clear state use random_walk, then alternating to a short move_forward progress state before returning to random exploration.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion with two simple plant automata.",
    "Use one policy specification with clear/search, short-progress, and one-shot turn-recovery states.",
    "Make all states total on uncontrollables and deterministic.",
    "Use random_walk in the initial clear exploration state, move_forward only in a dedicated short-progress state, and directed turns for ordinary obstacle recovery.",
    "Reserve full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort recovery state reached only from repeated front blockage."
  ],
